4. PROOF TARGETS SUGGESTED BY THE TREE VIEW
==============================================================================
A. The local dyadic endpoint theorem is a normalized Markov/Hecke kernel:
   every tree drop has total active residue mass exactly one.
B. The known nine-cover is a star current: one radial half-horosphere
   plus eight deep boundary eighth-horospheres.
C. The u=16 private-leaf proof is exceptional.  From u=32 onward, the
   all-lower local incidence graph has no private endpoints and has a
   nonempty 2-core, so the n=16 proof needs a global flow inequality.
D. A would-be disproof should look like a harmonic current on a truncated
   2-adic tree.  The conjectural obstruction is that primitive gcd-breaker
   speeds create positive divergence, visible as gap or endpoint leaves.
